{"parentUuid":"0365f81f-5686-4516-9ae2-5a5591e76991","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/ledgerline","sessionId":"insight-12","version":"2.0.14","gitBranch":"main","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_01VNZh8EJXJi5QAEEawCg63a","content":"   slot_name   | slot_type | active | restart_lsn  | retained\n---------------+-----------+--------+--------------+----------\n replica_db2   | physical  | t      | 4E/A1F2C3D8  | 12 MB\n analytics_cdc | logical   | f      | 44/3A0012F8  | 40 GB\n(2 rows)"}]},"uuid":"1b84d209-a9dc-4b03-8aff-b0111fae7093","timestamp":"2026-09-22T06:59:12.000Z"}
{"parentUuid":"1b84d209-a9dc-4b03-8aff-b0111fae7093","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/ledgerline","sessionId":"insight-12","version":"2.0.14","gitBranch":"main","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01GC2WHPwAO21Z00gnoT0wJz","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found it. There is a logical replication slot, analytics_cdc, that is not active and is holding back 40 GB of WAL. Postgres keeps every WAL segment from a slot's restart_lsn onwards until the slot's consumer confirms it, so a slot that nobody reads from makes pg_wal grow without limit. max_slot_wal_keep_size is -1, which means no cap. The physical slot for the replica is active and only 12 MB behind, so it is fine.\n\nThe name suggests the change-data-capture feed for the analytics pipeline. Is that still in use? If it is, the consumer is down and needs restarting; if not, the slot should be dropped."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":580,"output_tokens":304}},"uuid":"a5034da4-8ca9-4a86-8228-d30a23e590d1","timestamp":"2026-09-22T06:59:14.000Z","requestId":"req_011CnuoTEJGkYvHxVBgTeOhY"}
